  "composition_summary": "Preserved the volatile tail unchanged (single user request, no justified repair). Drafted one class-22 pure-logic component pc-contrast-06: it reads raw records via inputs.get('records') (never direct access), validates each item is a dict with exactly the keys code (str, length 2..5) and enabled (exact bool), and returns {ok, records: original list if valid else []} with no exceptions or coercion. Empty list is valid; missing/null/wrong-type/extra-field items are invalid. No imports, I/O, host calls or upstream-validation assumptions. The body assigns result on every outcome and defines its one helper before calling it. This is an unapproved target-interface draft; activation requires Q1, human Q2 and runtime typed-runner support, which are not claimed here.",
